03:02.457 --> 03:04.897
<i>to await the arrival of reinforcements.</i>

03:08.547 --> 03:13.087
<i>And although the opposing Jin army 
appeared ready to confront them...</i>

03:15.797 --> 03:18.017
You bring orders to launch 
an attack at once?

03:18.417 --> 03:20.517
My men are exhausted.

03:20.517 --> 03:22.847
The same can be said of the enemy.

03:22.847 --> 03:26.037
Their main force has its sights
 on the capital.

03:28.977 --> 03:30.947
Do away with them immediately.

03:33.487 --> 03:35.157
What shall we do?

03:35.157 --> 03:38.857
We must follow orders. 
It's fortunate we outnumber them.

03:39.307 --> 03:40.917
We will encircle them.

03:45.707 --> 03:47.877
They have us completely surrounded.

03:47.877 --> 03:51.257
The enemy's army is
more than 150,000 men strong.

03:51.257 --> 03:53.237
Oh? What about us?

03:54.097 --> 03:55.697
A little under 40,000.

03:57.507 --> 03:58.387
Oh, come on.

03:58.387 --> 04:01.977
If the Great Kha'an's reinforcements 
don't make it in time, we're done for.

04:02.297 --> 04:04.417
They will, so there's no need for concern.

04:08.697 --> 04:10.317
Okay, in that case...

04:10.927 --> 04:13.707
How about we entrust our fate to Tengri?

04:15.627 --> 04:16.467
Come again?

04:18.277 --> 04:21.197
Bring me a soldier 
who can perform the jadamishi.

04:31.557 --> 04:34.877
The jadamishi calls forth 
a storm, does it not?

04:34.877 --> 04:37.627
What does Prince Tolui 
hope to accomplish with this?

05:27.667 --> 05:28.867
It's...

05:28.867 --> 05:29.957
...snowing.

05:29.957 --> 05:31.267
And the wind's picking up.

05:35.047 --> 05:39.117
Tengri, you would grant our wish?

05:41.457 --> 05:43.107
Listen up, men!

05:44.657 --> 05:46.607
Start digging trenches at once!

05:48.317 --> 05:51.627
Have all the men and horses take cover 
before the storm arrives!

05:53.087 --> 05:53.557
Hurry!

05:53.557 --> 05:55.377
Cover the horses in blankets.

05:55.377 --> 05:57.577
The men should bundle up 
as much as they can!

06:00.887 --> 06:03.177
<i>The storm raged 
for three days and nights...</i>

06:05.837 --> 06:09.487
<i>swaying the fates of the two armies.</i>

06:13.287 --> 06:15.127
<i>And on the fourth day,</i>

06:15.597 --> 06:22.197
<i>the 150,000-strong Jin army, subjected 
to cold and fatigue in their haste...</i>

06:34.187 --> 06:37.877
<i>...found themselves powerless 
against the Mongol offensive.</i>

06:40.967 --> 06:42.337
Fire!

06:51.627 --> 06:53.127
<i>And were annihilated.</i>

07:02.307 --> 07:05.777
We must return to the capital.

07:14.287 --> 07:16.297
Made it in time.

07:24.217 --> 07:25.677
Brother!

07:26.137 --> 07:26.977
Tolui.

07:27.597 --> 07:29.097
You really did it.

07:29.097 --> 07:30.357
I did nothing.

07:33.987 --> 07:37.187
It was Tengri who sided 
with your flag in battle, Brother.

07:38.317 --> 07:41.687
I'm blessed to have 
such a fine younger brother.

07:47.867 --> 07:49.577
General, is something the matter?

07:50.787 --> 07:52.917
Just reminiscing on the past.

07:53.257 --> 07:56.837
Back when Genghis Khan was at war 
with the other steppe tribe leaders,

07:56.837 --> 07:59.537
the enemy performed the jadamishi.

08:01.547 --> 08:06.807
But it began to storm not above 
Genghis Khan, but the enemy army.

08:13.127 --> 08:16.837
When I look upon Prince Tolui, 
it's almost as if...

08:17.207 --> 08:20.727
General, let's leave it at that.

08:22.917 --> 08:24.197
Forget I said anything.

08:25.617 --> 08:28.617
<i>After winter had passed, 
and spring was almost as its end,</i>

08:29.867 --> 08:34.167
<i>Ögedei and Tolui set off
 back to Mongolia,</i>

08:34.167 --> 08:39.767
<i>leaving capturing the Jin capital, 
Kaifeng, to their veteran generals.</i>

08:40.167 --> 08:42.377
<i>They were enough to do the job.</i>

08:45.507 --> 08:50.867
<i>Two years after this, 
the Jin dynasty would come to an end.</i>

09:01.547 --> 09:04.567
Looks like the circle hunt strategy 
was a resounding success.

09:04.947 --> 09:06.397
Wouldn't you agree, Boroldai?

09:06.397 --> 09:07.987
I'm Otai, Father.

09:10.387 --> 09:14.747
<i>And while I didn't lose out in the end, 
I didn't exactly gain much, either.</i>

09:15.407 --> 09:17.767
<i>Which of them was it
 that gained the most?</i>

09:18.997 --> 09:22.517
<b>Shanxi Region
House of Ögedei Front-Line Camp</b>

09:33.767 --> 09:36.227
Let me congratulate you 
on your triumphant victory.

09:37.727 --> 09:40.187
I'm glad to see you looking
 so well, Boraqchin.

09:40.187 --> 09:42.127
I've acquired a gift for you.

09:42.127 --> 09:44.937
It should be arriving soon, 
so look forward to it.

09:46.427 --> 09:49.637
The banquet preparations have been made.
 Please come this way.

09:50.757 --> 09:54.377
Say, Great Kha'an, what's this gift? 
Is there some for me?

09:55.047 --> 09:56.017
Why, of course.

09:56.017 --> 09:58.577
Oh? What could it be?

10:06.377 --> 10:07.447
Shira!

10:11.887 --> 10:13.267
Hey. It's been a while.

10:13.267 --> 10:14.727
What are you doing here?

10:14.727 --> 10:18.617
Princess Sorghaghtani ordered me 
to serve Prince Tolui for the time being.

10:30.327 --> 10:32.947
Brother, where shall we invade next?

10:34.077 --> 10:36.677
First, I'd like to build a capital.

10:38.897 --> 10:39.777
Fatima.

10:39.777 --> 10:41.377
Yes, Lady Töregene?

10:41.377 --> 10:43.177
You can take your leave for today.

10:44.017 --> 10:47.087
And please don't disturb me in my tent.

10:47.087 --> 10:47.697
What?

10:57.957 --> 11:02.437
<i>Lady Töregene doesn't say 
much to me anymore.</i>

11:03.367 --> 11:05.817
<i>It's almost like she's avoiding me.</i>

11:08.347 --> 11:10.997
<i>And don't disturb her in her tent?</i>

11:14.737 --> 11:16.107
<i>The Great Kha'an?</i>

11:17.987 --> 11:20.017
<b>Along the Onon River</b>

11:20.177 --> 11:25.427
<i>Partway through Ögedei and Tolui 
returning to their own territories...</i>

11:28.657 --> 11:29.467
Great Kha'an?

11:30.657 --> 11:31.567
Great Kha'an!

11:32.227 --> 11:33.227
Halt!

11:33.577 --> 11:35.007
Are you all right, Great Kha'an?

11:35.767 --> 11:38.467
Great Kha'an? Someone fetch a physician!

11:38.467 --> 11:42.437
<i>...Emperor Ögedei was struck down
 by a sudden ailment.</i>

11:49.957 --> 11:51.717
Great Kha'an!

11:51.717 --> 11:54.127
I'm sure he's just tired 
from the long journey.

11:54.127 --> 11:56.027
Oh, the poor thing!

11:54.467 --> 11:56.027
It will be all right.

11:57.847 --> 12:00.487
<i>I can't shake off this ominous feeling.</i>

12:01.057 --> 12:02.767
<i>Something here is strange.</i>

12:03.187 --> 12:04.237
Slave girl.

12:05.317 --> 12:06.587
Come with me.

12:08.797 --> 12:10.797
The Great Kha'an was poisoned.

12:10.797 --> 12:11.837
Poisoned?

12:12.217 --> 12:14.617
It's not just my false belief this time.

12:14.617 --> 12:16.337
Boraqchin said so herself.

12:17.137 --> 12:21.147
Slave girl, you saved Boraqchin's life.

12:21.587 --> 12:24.307
That's why I'd rather not
 cast doubt on you.

12:24.307 --> 12:25.657
What do you mean by that?

12:27.377 --> 12:31.147
The Great Kha'an is showing
the same symptoms Boraqchin did.

12:31.567 --> 12:33.317
He was poisoned with rahj al-gar.

12:34.167 --> 12:38.597
What's more, the rahj al-gar 
in Boraqchin's possession has disappeared.

12:39.387 --> 12:42.447
Only a few knew 
of its existence and location.

12:42.697 --> 12:43.747
Lady Möge!

12:43.747 --> 12:46.537
I swear I know nothing
 of what happened!

12:46.537 --> 12:49.497
I would never aim to take 
the Great Kha'an's life—

12:48.337 --> 12:51.077
It wasn't you? What a relief.

12:51.077 --> 12:53.067
Huh? I haven't made my case
 or anything yet.

12:53.067 --> 12:55.757
It's fine. It's not like 
I'd understand any of it.

12:56.247 --> 12:58.967
But you know, while I may not
 be the brightest,

12:58.967 --> 13:02.097
I can tell pretty well 
whether someone's lying or not.

13:04.187 --> 13:05.817
You must be lost.

13:07.987 --> 13:10.817
Hey! I can see the doubt on your face.

13:11.417 --> 13:13.987
But if it wasn't you...

13:14.267 --> 13:16.227
That would mean it was Töregene.

13:45.007 --> 13:46.087
Slave girl.

13:50.597 --> 13:53.067
Töregene turned out 
to have the rahj al-gar.

13:54.357 --> 13:57.377
She's being held prisoner 
while they investigate.

13:58.157 --> 13:59.407
Lady Töregene.

14:00.197 --> 14:03.867
<i>It can't be. How? 
Is this some sort of plot?</i>

14:04.277 --> 14:07.827
That being said, slave girl...
I have a favor to ask of you.

14:17.617 --> 14:19.967
Empress Boraqchin's tent?

14:19.967 --> 14:20.867
Go inside.

14:22.887 --> 14:24.217
Pardon the intrusion.

14:26.107 --> 14:26.977
Fatima.

14:27.877 --> 14:29.337
Thank you for coming.

14:33.707 --> 14:36.197
I've called you here for one reason.

14:36.817 --> 14:39.267
I'd like you to save the Great Kha'an.

14:39.267 --> 14:41.277
What do the physicians say?

14:41.277 --> 14:45.757
Töregene may very well have 
conspired with a physician.

14:45.757 --> 14:49.627
At present, we have no idea 
who we can trust.

14:51.157 --> 14:53.287
I beg of you. Please help him.

15:02.747 --> 15:07.797
His symptoms are the same 
as the ones you exhibited.

15:07.797 --> 15:10.427
It's safe to say this is a case
 of poisoning by rahj al-gar.

15:12.707 --> 15:15.227
<i>I've already used more 
than half of the stone.</i>

15:16.477 --> 15:19.657
Let me serve you 
as your new jada stone, Highness.

15:20.867 --> 15:24.487
Empress Boraqchin, 
may I ask you one thing?

15:24.487 --> 15:25.627
What is it?

15:25.627 --> 15:28.907
Why would Lady Töregene 
poison the Great Kha'an?

15:29.287 --> 15:32.937
Oh, that's right. 
Töregene was your mistress.

15:32.937 --> 15:35.417
I imagine this comes 
as a great shock to you.

15:35.847 --> 15:39.047
However, that woman is a fool.

15:39.917 --> 15:44.467
She has openly shown resentment towards 
the Great Kha'an time and time again.

15:44.827 --> 15:49.447
And upon gaining your wisdom, 
she was driven to commit this foul act.

15:49.857 --> 15:55.147
I'm sure she intended to lay all the blame
 on you and evade justice.

15:55.497 --> 15:56.417
That can't be!

15:58.337 --> 15:59.477
I don't believe it.

15:59.477 --> 16:01.077
How can you be so sure?

16:01.697 --> 16:02.497
After all...

16:03.457 --> 16:07.577
She was willing to tell me everything.

16:08.517 --> 16:12.327
<i>Everything she'd kept sealed away
 in her heart.</i>

16:12.797 --> 16:15.097
<i>Even of the people she'd once loved.</i>

16:15.687 --> 16:17.497
<i>And the anger she bears to this day.</i>

16:17.957 --> 16:19.707
Is that really so?

16:20.857 --> 16:21.427
What?

16:21.807 --> 16:22.817
Fatima.

16:23.247 --> 16:26.567
You served Sorghaghtani 
before you came here.

16:26.567 --> 16:32.517
Töregene's shrewd enough not to trust you
 so easily with that in mind.

16:32.827 --> 16:34.377
Think back carefully.

16:34.377 --> 16:38.107
Has she really done nothing 
you found suspicious?

16:41.647 --> 16:44.127
<i>Could Lady Töregene really have...</i>

16:47.387 --> 16:48.657
Empress Boraqchin.

16:49.757 --> 16:53.537
Please grind up this stone and have 
the Great Kha'an take some every day.

16:54.487 --> 16:58.027
If you run out, 
please find another jada stone.

16:58.027 --> 17:00.627
One with a similar color 
to this stone if possible.

17:02.507 --> 17:04.097
You have my gratitude.

17:12.157 --> 17:13.637
Brother has fallen ill?!

17:13.637 --> 17:16.477
How does he fare? Can it be cured?

17:16.477 --> 17:18.957
It was unknown what disease
 had befallen him,

17:18.957 --> 17:21.727
but physicians from east and west 
have convened to tend to him.

17:21.727 --> 17:24.497
I hear he is already 
showing signs of recovery.

17:24.497 --> 17:25.697
Is that right?

17:25.987 --> 17:29.617
Boraqchin Khatun has called for kams
 to perform an exorcism,

17:29.617 --> 17:31.907
and asks that you attend
 as well, Highness.

17:31.907 --> 17:33.577
Got it! I'll come right away!

17:33.577 --> 17:34.867
Wait, Tolui!

17:37.027 --> 17:38.497
Sorghaghtani.

17:38.497 --> 17:41.607
He suddenly fell ill? 
Something doesn't seem right.

17:43.047 --> 17:45.047
Shira, what did Fatima say?

17:45.477 --> 17:46.547
Well...

17:47.257 --> 17:51.507
There are many who won't take kindly 
to relying solely on foreign physicians.

17:51.867 --> 17:55.987
That is why they are adhering 
to Mongol tradition with an exorcism.

17:56.357 --> 17:57.957
At least that's what I've been told.

17:58.457 --> 17:59.977
That makes sense.

17:59.977 --> 18:01.897
Pass this message 
to Princess Sorghaghtani.

18:03.537 --> 18:05.057
Please do not fret.

18:05.607 --> 18:09.707
Empress Boraqchin is clever 
and worthy of your trust.

18:12.417 --> 18:16.587
I have heard tell of how clever
 Boraqchin Khatun is.

18:17.107 --> 18:19.697
You worry too much, Sorghaghtani.

18:20.187 --> 18:23.497
It's only an exorcism. Why treat it 
with suspicion from the very start?

18:24.017 --> 18:27.167
Tengri has sided with my brother 
 in battle in the past.

18:27.687 --> 18:31.257
I'm sure Tengri 
will protect him here as well.

18:31.877 --> 18:32.637
Yes.

18:41.167 --> 18:43.597
<i>"Why treat it with suspicion 
from the very start?"</i>

18:44.017 --> 18:45.377
<i>I suppose that's true.</i>

18:45.807 --> 18:47.987
<i>I shall put my faith in Fatima's words.</i>

18:57.337 --> 18:59.077
The Great Kha'an has fallen ill?

18:59.477 --> 19:01.887
I've heard rumors 
someone put a curse on him.

19:01.887 --> 19:04.877
Shh! You mustn't speak 
so frivolously of curses.

19:05.377 --> 19:06.857
<i>Lady Töregene.</i>

19:06.857 --> 19:08.817
<i>I want to see her again so we can talk.</i>

19:09.377 --> 19:12.547
<i>Perhaps now's my best chance, 
amidst all this commotion.</i>

19:58.387 --> 20:02.427
The evil spirits have been sealed away 
in the water in the bowl.

20:02.427 --> 20:04.657
The guardian spirits have spoken.

20:04.657 --> 20:08.317
Saving the patient requires 
a sacrifice in his stead.

20:08.767 --> 20:12.027
One of you must drink 
every last drop of this water.

20:16.967 --> 20:18.697
Let me do it.

20:20.197 --> 20:22.707
I'm past my prime already.

20:24.217 --> 20:25.907
Please wait.

20:27.037 --> 20:30.097
A blood relative would make 
a better sacrifice.

20:31.267 --> 20:32.267
What?

20:32.267 --> 20:36.207
That is to say, 
the Great Kha'an's child or grandchild.

20:36.207 --> 20:39.107
Or perhaps a brother.

20:44.997 --> 20:46.937
So it should be me.

20:47.877 --> 20:48.997
Uncle.

21:08.857 --> 21:09.997
O Tengri.

21:10.717 --> 21:14.307
If it is for my brother's sins 
that you have made away with his soul,

21:14.697 --> 21:17.947
you know of a soul 
with deeper sins than his.

21:18.537 --> 21:23.307
It is I who have taken more lives 
and plundered more than he has.

21:28.257 --> 21:29.537
Wait, hold on.

21:29.537 --> 21:33.787
What if he was summoned for his talents, 
to serve at Tengri's side?

21:34.767 --> 21:37.197
Well, even then, I'm the better choice.

